WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.400
CHEERING AND APPLAUSE

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.440
Thank you. Slightly
overestimated how tall I am there.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.200
To my mum...

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.360
I knew from a very young
age that I was different.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.280
We both did.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.480
The way I'd sort my toys...

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.080
That I'd insist on different
plates for different foods...

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.440
And birthday parties
made me anxious.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.880
And, by the time I was
four years old,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.280
I became so sure that if I didn't
hide my differences,

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.040
people wouldn't like me.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.880
So, I became a version of myself

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.320
I thought those around me
would accept.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.720
I became a mimic,
copying other people,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.760
imitating normal behaviour,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.320
and suppressing anything weird.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.360
For most people, these rules come
naturally, automatically.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.400
Their faces match their voices,
match their feelings.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.560
But I had to think about every
little thing.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.160
In the end, I put so much effort
into this mask of normality

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.240
that nobody could even tell
that I had one.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.560
When you're autistic, masking,
camouflaging,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.880
it's a survival strategy.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.240
It's to avoid judgment
or avoid bullying.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.560
It's a way to fit
into the non-autistic world.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.040
I have masked with everybody
in my life...

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.760
..including you, Mum.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.120
I wanted to be the perfect child.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.440
I wanted to make you proud.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.360
But now...I'm tired.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.480
It's exhausting pretending
to be normal all the time.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.200
I'm beginning to think

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.720
it might be time to embrace my
authentic self,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.240
to show you the
things you don't normally see.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.680
But I'm scared.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.600
I'm worried that
if I'm quiet and still,

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.760
and my face doesn't
match my feelings,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.320
then you'll think
that I'm being rude.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.600
I'm worried that if you see me
rocking back and forth,

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:53.760
or flapping my hands, then
you'll think that I'm not OK.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.440
And I'm worried that if you see me
silent, unable to speak,

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.760
you'll think that I need fixing.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.000
It might not come easily
for me straight away,

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.080
but I'm ready to be myself.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.360
I hope you won't be disappointed.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.240
I love you always.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.160
Your daughter, Flo.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.520
You all right?

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.080
- Love you.
- I love you.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.720
I want to scoop up
the five-year-old you.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.040
- Mm-hm. Me too.
- And say it's OK.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.040
- Yeah?
- And if we could turn the clock

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.600
back, and I knew what I know today,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.880
it would be... Maybe I would
have been able to give you

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.040
some reassurance about,
it's OK.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.920
It's absolutely OK, you know?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.400
- Yeah.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.200
All through my childhood
and my teenage life

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.320
and my adult life,

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.120
you've been so accepting...

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.520
I'm going to cry.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.520
..of everything
that I am.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.360
- Because you're lovely.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.280
I'm all right.
THEY LAUGH

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.400
But, like...

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.760
-  It's, er...
- It's scary being different.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.920
It wasn't anything about you.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.920
It was the world, really.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.280
- No, but I...

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.920
Please, you know, you don't have to
mask in front of me any more.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.080
- That's why... that's why I
wanted this video for you.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.520
- Yeah.
- I wanted this film

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.840
to tell you that.
But it's been really hard to go,

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.880
"I've always been kind of acting."

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.040
Yeah.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.880
I didn't expect to get snotty.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.280
I know. Do you want a tissue?

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.880
Thank you.

